  "history": "Founded in 2005 in Boston by Todd Dagres, Santo Politi, Paul Conway and Bijan Sabet with a $265M first fund, Spark Capital became one of the defining consumer-internet investors of the 2000s and 2010s: the Series A or B backer of Twitter (2008), Tumblr, Foursquare, Warby Parker, Wayfair, Oculus (sold to Facebook for $2B in 2014), Slack, Plaid (seed, 2013) and Cruise (Series A, 2015), with a Start@Spark seed program (2009) that funded first checks out of the main fund. A growth practice launched in 2014 (Spark Capital Growth Fund, $374M) added late positions in Affirm, Coinbase, Discord, Marqeta, Snap and Kalshi, and the firm led Anthropic's $450M Series C in 2023. One partnership runs both practices from San Francisco, New York and Boston. Nine early-stage funds (Spark Capital IX closed at $1.0B in 2026) and six growth funds (Growth Fund VI closed at $2.33B in 2026) sit under one exempt reporting adviser (CRD 161231) whose private funds held $15.6B of gross assets at the 2025 fiscal year end.",
  "investment_concept": "Spark Capital backs founders from the first check through growth, investing in consumer, enterprise software, fintech, crypto, hardware and AI companies with early-stage and growth funds run by one partnership.",
